The woman gives me my papers back.
She smiles.
"Welcome to Denmark," she says.
"Thank you very much," I say.
I am happy.
Now everything is in order.
I have a CPR number.
It is very important.
I also have a Danish phone number.
And I have an address.
I have everything.
I am a little proud.
I smile too.
Now my new life in Copenhagen begins.
